Round 50 is complete and live at stamp 1786139194.

**What the round did.** The queue item was B9's second consumer: `battle.js` still wind-scaled ship speeds through its own polar model — `btPolarSpeed(curve, rel) × (0.55 + force·0.09)`, with no beat gate, no oar floor, no engine rule. That model is deleted, not patched. The Action now compiles each fleet's polar once at open with route.js's own `compilePolar` and asks route.js's `polarSpeed` every frame, converting the record's Beaufort force to a true wind by v = 0.836·B^1.5. The beat computation moved into its own `polarBeat` in route.js, so the battle's helm asks the same gate the speed model enforces: a ship whose direct course would make no way falls to the nearer beat limb, which is what a helmsman with a station to windward does. Any future galley action — Salamis, Lepanto, Myeongnyang all have battle cards — is now unblocked at the engine level.

**How it was verified.** Old-vs-new measured at 192 (vessel, force, heading) points through the page's own functions: the trireme's calm went 2.0 → 5.4 kn (Olympias's cruise held at every heading), her force-7 headwind went 4.4 → 0.6 kn (the old model had a near-gale on the nose *helping* her), and the sail fleets lost their impossible windward ghosting while shifting −10% to +18% abaft the gate. Unfrozen, all 40 Armada ships make way on days 0, 3 and 9, including Portland's NE wind. Three new audit rules — a calm must not slow a floored hull through the *running* model, `btPolarSpeed` stays dead, the three shared globals stay reachable — each proven by in-page break-and-restore firing exactly where it should, then 25/25 clean. The proof also caught a real fragility: blanking `polarBeat` threw the audit before the rule naming it could run, so the calm-floor rule now guards on all three globals.

**Frames and deploy.** All 37 ratchet frames within tolerance, zero movers — correct for a behavioral change under a frozen clock — run foreground, frame by frame. The action frame was captured and inspected: fleets hull-down at their real 7 km separation, force-6 swell, the card holding 30 July 1588. Two servers on :8149 again; both checked, both serve `web/`. Pushed in b0eaeba, live stamp verified 1786137697 → 1786139194 with the live battle.js confirmed carrying the fix, deploy note committed in 3e4b45a. HANDOFF.md leaves the carried items queue and notes the galley-action unblock for the next round.
